<h1>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Gap @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</h1>


<p>
    Everything you need to work with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-gaps-*</span>, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-row-gap-*</span>, and <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-col-gap-*</span> CSS classes: the utility classes provided, the strongly-typed <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Gap</span> C# object
    used to apply them, and the supporting enum used to select a gap size.
</p>

<h2 class="page-heading">Overview</h2>

<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Gap</span> is a <b>utility class</b>, not a BEM component class like <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">GridRow</span> or <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">FlexContent</span>.
    Rather than describing a block, element, or its variants, each method sets a single CSS gap property to a fixed value. Utility classes are flat
    and single-purpose by design, so they can be freely combined with each other and with any other class - including component classes - on the same element.
</p>
<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">gap</span>, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">row-gap</span> and <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">column-gap</span> behave identically whether applied within a
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-flex-content</span> container or a <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-grid-row</span> container, so <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Gap</span> is shared between both rather than
    duplicated per layout mode.
</p>
<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">SetGaps</span> sets both the row and column gap at once. Combine it with <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">SetRowGap</span> or
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">SetColGap</span> on the same element to override just one axis - e.g. apply <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Four)</span> alongside
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Gap.SetRowGap(UnitGapSize.Two)</span> to get a gap of 4 on both axes except the row gap, which becomes 2.
</p>

<section>
    <h2 id="c#-classes" class="page-heading">C# API</h2>
    <p>
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Gap</span> provides utility classes that set the gap between the children of a flex or grid container.
    </p>
    <section>
        <h3 id="gap-class" class="code-table__heading">Gap class</h3>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="gap-class">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Return</th>
                        <th scope="col">Static Method</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize unitGapSize)</td>
                        <td>Gets the class that sets both the row and column gap, between a container's children.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Gap.SetRowGap(UnitGapSize unitGapSize)</td>
                        <td>Gets the class that sets the row gap only, between a container's children.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Gap.SetColGap(UnitGapSize unitGapSize)</td>
                        <td>Gets the class that sets the column gap only, between a container's children.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>

